cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Future B: Exact-corrected delayed acceptance and validation tools for first-principles diagrammatic Monte Carlo"
message: "The core methods study is closed (v1.0.0 science frozen); v1.3.x adds a maintained FEP-DMC research toolkit. Cite the software record and the upstream FEP-DMC paper separately."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wong
    given-names: Kawa
    alias: DarrenWongKaWa
version: "1.3.3"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/DarrenWongKaWa/future-b"
abstract: >
  Methods study (closed at v1.0.0, science frozen) of exact-corrected
  analytic delayed acceptance (P1) in Luo EZ / Perturbo FEP-DMC for the
  LiF electron polaron, with a maintained v1.3.x FEP-DMC research toolkit
  (future_b.fepdmc) and native findings.
  The public snapshot is a research archive (Python algebra, Fortran
  excerpts, frozen records). It does not ship the historical R1
  evaluator, a native one-click plugin, or a 1% ground-state result.
keywords:
  - diagrammatic Monte Carlo
  - electron-phonon
  - polaron
  - delayed acceptance
  - LiF
references:
  - type: article
    title: "First-principles diagrammatic Monte Carlo for electron-phonon interactions and polarons"
    authors:
      - family-names: Luo
        given-names: Yao
      - family-names: Park
        given-names: Jinsoo
      - family-names: Bernardi
        given-names: Marco
    journal: Nature Physics
    year: 2025
    volume: "21"
    pages: "1275"
    doi: "10.1038/s41567-025-02954-1"
